  "name": "zendnn-skills",
  "description": "Single entry point for working with the ZenDNN library (zendnnl). Routes each request to the matching sub-skill, collects shared inputs once, runs multi-step requests in order and reports one result. Covers building zendnnl, building vLLM for CPU against upstream oneDNN and ZenDNN without zentorch, developing and optimizing an operator, reviewing an operator change or a ZenDNN pull request, running gtests, benchmarking with BenchDNN, measuring a machine's ceilings and rating matmul calls against them (a roofline), and keeping C++ and CMake changes working on the native Windows (MSVC) build. Use for any task that involves changing ZenDNN's C++ or CMake, or building, testing, benchmarking, configuring, integrating or reviewing ZenDNN. When no sub-skill covers the task, it says so and works only from the repository's own documentation.",
